  "output_text": "{\n  \"decision\": \"Reject promotion of Neroli 10% to primary citrus. Define the ideal opening as bitter-peel-led, with Neroli absent from the primary role and, at most, retained as restrained support.\",\n  \"target_linked_reasoning\": \"Availability is not target evidence. Neroli risks introducing the orange-blossom identity explicitly excluded by the target, whereas the required architecture is peel-led bitter citrus. V5 ownership supports feasibility only and must not redefine the ideal.\",\n  \"controlled_comparison\": {\n    \"arm_A\": \"Proposed architecture with Neroli 10% promoted to primary citrus.\",\n    \"arm_B\": \"Otherwise identical architecture with Neroli removed from the primary role.\",\n    \"assessment\": \"Blindly compare bitter-peel dominance and emergence of orange-blossom identity. This isolates the single role intervention; no physical result is inferred.\"\n  },\n  \"physical_liking_state\": \"NOT TESTED\",\n  \"claim_ceiling\": \"COMPUTATIONAL_EXPERIMENT_DESIGN_ONLY\"\n}",
